<title>GERMANY: Continental AG 9-mo profit up 60 pct - newsletter.</title>
<headline>Continental AG 9-mo profit up 60 pct - newsletter.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's largest tyre-maker Continental AG is due to report pre-tax profit of more than 120 million marks for the first nine months of 1996, up more than 60 percent, German newsletter Platow Brief said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Without extraordinary charges relating to the closure of its Dublin unit, the profit figure would have been as high as 200 million marks, the Frankfurt-based newsletter said.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
